  "explains": "requireAuth in src/middleware/auth.ts accepts a session. src/routes/orders.ts imports it and names it in two route calls: router.get(\"/:id\", requireAuth, getOrder) and router.post(\"/\", requireAuth, createOrder). Those two routes are reached: GET /api/v1/orders/{id} and POST /api/v1/orders. The other statements of the router do not name it. The client calls orderUrl(orderId), so the edge to GET /api/v1/orders/{id} and OrderScreen follow; nothing in the client calls POST /api/v1/orders.",
  "complete_for": [
    "changed_symbol",
    "route",
    "screen",
    "http_edge",
    "finding"
  ],
  "must_find": [
